// Slint embeds, for the software renderer, only the glyphs of characters it can see in the .slint
// sources (plus ASCII). Names and questions arrive at run time, so this lists the rest of Latin-1 and
// Latin Extended-A (accents) and common punctuation: it is never shown. Characters outside the fonts
// (CJK, emoji, Greek in Sora) have no glyph and draw as blanks.
